  "whatIsThis": {
    "intro": "The frame is the skeleton: the one part with no electrons in it, and the one that takes the crashes. T700 carbon plates and arms, a 226 mm wheelbase for 5-inch props, 30.5 and 20 mm stack mounting in the middle, 16x16 motor mounts at the arm tips, and an aluminium camera mount at the nose. It decides what fits: stack height, camera width, prop size. Less obviously, it decides what your gyro feels. Every arm has a resonant frequency, and flex and vibration land straight in the flight controller's filters, so stiffness is a flight characteristic, not a cosmetic one. OpenFC Lite and OpenESC drop in without spacers.",
    "needs": [
      "A flight controller and ESC stack bolted in the middle",
      "Four motors and props at the arm tips",
      "A receiver, camera and VTX",
      "A LiPo and a battery strap",
      "A radio and goggles on the ground"
    ],
    "fit": "Everything else mounts to it; it turns a bag of boards into an aircraft.",
